# What the standby discard model stands for. .agents/skills/standby-discard says how to keep it true:
# its Coverage record maps each model action to the code below.
#
# sync: the commit whose code the model was last confirmed to describe. Move it only as the
# skill's step 1 and full run say. 38bd550c95 is main when SLNT-1053 moved it: mend#1727's squash,
# whose covered changes (SLNT-1044) the line before already accounted for, and nothing else in the
# covered files. SLNT-1053 changed the model with the code: the launch's re-plan is asked again
# and, when no ask answered, the standby's own status decides adoption (AReplanOk, AReplanFail,
# AIdentify); a session's drain discards a claimed standby whose re-plan never took and in which no
# process ever ran (discardStandbyNeverClaimed: GLook, GIdentify,
# GDiscard, KeptRetry), with joins modelled (JEnter, JLook). SessionProcessesRepo joins the
# covered files for existsForWorkspace. Its second round (the box check of mend#1741) added the
# owner's Stop during the asks (Stop, AgentStarts) and bound the session's channel again before
# the cold launch, which no action models (the channel is not in the model).
# c34dea602e is main when SLNT-1063 moved it: SLNT-1053's squash (d1039eaf1d), which changed the
# model with the code, and nothing else in the covered files. SLNT-1063 (mend#1756) then changed
# engine.ts only outside the covered functions: every workspace create's env and each person's
# process env carry MEND_ORIGIN, and the workspace note names it; no action models either. The
# full TLC run on its head, dde8b8acd6, had every row as expected.
# 591a9e6e3b is the SLNT-895 feature branch on main after SLNT-1063, when it moved the line. Its
# covered changes deliver an imported conversation at a session's first protocol launch:
# conversationOf's home, launchProtocol's resume id and prepareImportedConversation. They make no
# hot-pool, claim, retire, drain or session-process call, so no action models them. Full TLC run at
# 591a9e6e3b: every row as expected.
sync 591a9e6e3b859d6959f848a2853df3aa04ab8a83

model StandbyDiscard.tla
model MCStandbyDiscard.tla
model check.sh

path packages/db/src/repos/hot-workspaces.ts
path packages/db/src/repos/session-processes.ts
path packages/sessions/src/engine.ts
path packages/sessions/src/capture-channel.ts

# How long check.sh may run on CI's four-core runner before formal.mjs stops it and fails
# naming this model (SLNT-1065). GitHub's four-core runner is not one speed: the full bounds took
# 57 minutes on a fast host (b192d2e2, `code` at 18M states generated a minute), and a slow host
# (nightly 44068746119, 12M a minute throughout) would have needed about 85. The budget is about 30%
# over the slow host, and CI's formal job allows 10 minutes more for setup.
budget-quick 10
budget-full 110
